    {
      "id": "05-04",
      "title": "Routing versus forwarding",
      "chapter": "The routing puzzle",
      "duration": 21.166666666666668,
      "narration": "Routing works out the useful choices. Forwarding uses those choices to move actual packets, one hop at a time. Think planning your trip first, then following the directions. We need both parts to reach the destination.",
      "bullets": [
